<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rezin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 732 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> · Also known as Rezin of Damascus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rezin was the last king of Aram-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, reigning in the mid-8th century BCE. He allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pekah">Pekah of Israel</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahaz">Ahaz</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syro-ephraimite-war">Syro-Ephraimite War</a>, prompting Ahaz to seek help from Tiglath-Pileser III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>. The Assyrians took Damascus in 732 BCE, executed Rezin and made his kingdom a province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rezin.jpg" alt="Rezin" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Wolgemut · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Rezin_as_he_is_protrayed_in_the_Liber_Chronicarum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
